  "description": "I am writing to seek your advice and formally request Listed Building Consent for external redecoration works to The White House, 155 Old Kent Road, London SE1 5UT, a Grade II listed building (List Entry Number: 1385736).\n\nWe wish to restore the rendered façade to its historically documented white colour, as recorded in the Historic England photograph dated 23 June 2001. This would match the building's traditional identity and name, \"The White House,\" and maintain its architectural character within the local streetscape.\n\nProposal details:\n- Paint product: Dulux Weathershield All Weather Purpose Smooth Masonry Paint – Pure Brilliant White (Product Code: 278458).\n- Preparation: Non-abrasive cleaning and preparation to protect the original render.\n- Finish: Microporous, breathable paint to allow the substrate to breathe and prevent moisture retention.\n- Justification: Return to a historically accurate colour, enhancing the heritage significance and visual prominence of the building.\n\n",
